<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <!-- Zero-dependency micro test runner, same pattern as PincabToolbox.Core.Tests: no xunit needed. -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\PincabToolbox.Core\PincabToolbox.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Linked source, not a ProjectReference to PincabToolbox.App: that project targets
      net8.0-windows with UseWPF, which needs the Windows Desktop SDK — unavailable in the cloud
      sandbox this test suite is written and run in (NU1100, same documented fact as everywhere
      else in this repo). Scenarios.cs and Loc.cs are the two files point 3 (CTO+Produit review,
      13/08) needed to test and the only App-owned decision-logic files with zero WPF dependency
      today, so they're compiled here directly by path instead of dragging in the whole App
      project. This is a deliberate, temporary bridge: point 5 (moving Scenarios.cs and
      decision-logic to PincabToolbox.Core) should retire this link-by-path setup in favour of a
      normal reference once Scenarios.cs lives in Core. If either file ever starts using a WPF
      type, this project will simply fail to build — a tripwire, not a bug, and the sign that this
      bridge needs to be reconsidered.

      MainWindow.xaml.cs's Build* methods are NOT here for a different, harder reason than WPF
      references: MainWindow is one half of a partial class whose other half (all the TxtRoot/
      BtnScan/... field declarations) is generated from MainWindow.xaml at compile time. There is
      no source file to link — testing it for real needs either the full WPF build (blocked here)
      or extracting its decision logic into WPF-free helpers first. See TRANSMISSION.md 13/08.
    -->
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\PincabToolbox.App\Scenarios.cs" Link="LinkedFromApp\Scenarios.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\PincabToolbox.App\Localization\Loc.cs" Link="LinkedFromApp\Loc.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
